     We will implement the new notification subsystem using **Redis Streams**.
     
     This decision is primarily driven by the team's existing familiarity[0m[2m with Redis, the low operational overhead of Redis Streams compared to Kafka, and the ability to meet the critical "exactly-once" delivery requirement for billing events. Redis Streams provides a robust, ordered, and persistent message queue with built-in consumer group[0m[2m support, all within an ecosystem the team already manages. Its relatively simple setup and integration will allow us to meet the aggressive two-week delivery timeline.
     
